<p class="mb-3">
<h3>Copilot code review is now available to the <%= @org_name%> organization</h3>
</p>
<p class="mb-3">
Members of the <%= @org_name %>  organization with a GitHub Copilot subscription can now enable access to GitHub Copilot code review (public preview).
</p>
<p class="mb-3">
To get started, an enterprise owner can enable public preview features by using the Copilot policy “Opt in to preview features.” Once enabled, organization administrators can turn on the feature for their organization using the same policy found under the Copilot policy settings. To learn more about this policy and how it works, visit our <%= link_to "documentation", Copilot::COPILOT_ENABLING_ORG_FEATURES_DOC %>.
</p>
<p class="mb-3">
There are three ways to get a review from Copilot:
</p>
<p class="mb-3">
<ul>
  <li><%= link_to "Tag Copilot as a pull request reviewer on GitHub.com", Copilot::CODE_REVIEW_REQUEST_DOCS_URL %> from the "Reviewers" menu</li>
  <li><%= link_to "Enable automatic reviews for new pull requests on GitHub.com", Copilot::CODE_REVIEW_AUTOMATIC_DOCS_URL %> using rulesets (admin permissions required)</li>
  <li><%= link_to "Use the \"Review Changes\" button in Visual Studio Code", Copilot::CODE_REVIEW_VS_CODE_DOCS_URL %>, available when drafting a commit in the "Source Control" tab</li>
</ul>
</p>

<p class="mb-3">
To get the most out of Copilot code review, we recommend that you enable automatic reviews for your repositories on GitHub.com. For more information on Copilot code review, head to the <%= link_to "docs", Copilot::CODE_REVIEW_DOCS_URL %>.
</p>
<p class="mb-3">
<% if @has_enterprise_access %>
Support for custom coding guidelines, allowing you to tailor Copilot's reviews to your codebase, is coming soon.
<% end %>
</p>
<p class="mb-3">
<h3>Taking Copilot's suggestions forward with Copilot Workspace on GitHub.com</h3>
</p>
<p class="mb-3">
Alongside Copilot code review, your users also have access to Copilot Workspace in the context of their pull requests, a new experience on GitHub.com where they can validate and tweak Copilot's suggestions before applying them to a branch.
</p>
<p class="mb-3">
To jump into Workspace, just click the "Open in Workspace" on a suggestion from Copilot code review on GitHub.com, or use the "Edit" button on any file. To learn more about Copilot Workspace, head to the <%= link_to "docs", Copilot::WORKSPACE_FOR_PRS_DOCS_URL %>.
</p>
<p class="mb-3">
<h3>Getting supporting and sharing your feedback</h3>
</p>
<p class="mb-3">
We'd love to hear feedback from you and your team so we can make Copilot code review and Copilot Workspace even better.
</p>
<p class="mb-3">
When you receive a comment from Copilot, you can give feedback directly with the 👍 and 👎 buttons.
</p>
<p class="mb-3">
You can also share your thoughts and get support in our discussions on the GitHub Community:
</p>
<p class="mb-3">
<%= link_to "Copilot code review feedback and support", Copilot::CODE_REVIEW_DISCUSSION_URL %><br>
<%= link_to "Copilot Workspace feedback and support", Copilot::COPILOT_WORKSPACE_DISCUSSION %>
</p>
<p class="mb-3">
Please note that use of Copilot code review and Copilot Workspace is subject to GitHub's <%= link_to "Pre-release License Terms", Copilot::PRE_RELEASE_TERMS %>.
</p>

<% content_for :footer_text do %>
You are receiving this email because you are an owner of the <% @org_name %> organization, and the organization signed up for the Copilot code review public preview.
<% end %>
